      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-77291",
      ":question/problem": "An owl is perched on the branch of a vertical tree. From its position, the owl spots a mouse and a lizard on the horizontal ground. The mouse is directly below the owl. If the owl is $6m$ from the lizard and the angle of depression from the owl to the lizard is $42^{\u2218}$, how far is the lizard from the mouse? Round your answer to the nearest tenth of a meter.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
